

You should probably install too:
* rust:
    * rustup       https://rustup.rs/
    * for bash completion run: `rustup completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/rustup`
    * and then: `rustup completions bash cargo >> ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/cargo`
* Alacritty:       https://github.com/alacritty/alacritty
* dunst
    * dunst 1.6.0 (esp. dunstify) is required for proper sound volume and brightness change notifications
        use https://github.com/dunst-project/dunst
    * install from package manager if recent enough, otherwise from GitHub https://github.com/dunst-project/dunst
* Simplenote:      https://github.com/Automattic/simplenote-electron/releases/
    * can't start? https://github.com/Automattic/simplenote-electron/issues/3096
* Obsidian:        https://obsidian.md/
    * prefer a native package if available for your distro
* nnn:             https://github.com/jarun/nnn/releases
* bat:             https://github.com/sharkdp/bat
* ExifTool:        https://exiftool.org/
* mpv:
    mpv may not suspend GNOME's Power Saving Settings if using Wayland resulting in screen saver turning off the monitor during video playback.
    A workaround is to add `gnome-session-inhibit` to the beginning of the `Exec=` line in `/usr/share/applications/mpv.desktop`.

On Fedora, configure `firewalld` / `firewall-config` instead of `ufw`.

